Comment: hd-pipes is based on hacks/glx/pipes.c of xscreensaver, which comes
 from xlockmore, by Marcelo F. Vianna, 1997, under the notice of the license
 pipes-c below, as it is in pipes.c. Its sources in pipes/ start with the
 same notice.
 .
 The flanges and bolts of its bolted elbows and the gauges and valves of its
 factory, in pipes/src/mesh.cpp, are measured from pipeobjs.c of
 xscreensaver, which also comes from xlockmore and was generated by lw2ogl. pipeobjs.c has no notice of its own; Debian
 files it under the notice of xscreensaver, by Jamie Zawinski, the license
 xscreensaver below.
 .
 The teapot of its factory is the Newell teapot of teapot.c of
 xscreensaver, by Mark J. Kilgard, 1994, with the notice of Silicon
 Graphics, 1993, the license teapot-c below. pipes/src/teapot.cpp holds its
 control points and patches, copied from teapot.c, and starts with that
 notice, as does pipes/src/teapot.hpp.
 .
 The binaries also hold the interface tables that wayland-scanner generates
 from two Wayland protocols: wlr-layer-shell, of wlr-protocols, and
 xdg-shell, of wayland-protocols. Their notices follow.

